{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>My judgments you shall do.</b> These are the matters stated in the Torah as מִשְׁפָּט — had they not been stated, they would have been worthy to be stated." "<b>And My statutes you shall keep.</b> Matters that are a decree of the King, against which the evil inclination argues: Why should we keep them? And the nations of the world argue against them — such as eating pork, wearing shaatnez, and the purification of the waters of the sin-offering. Therefore it says <b>I am YHWH</b> — I decreed them upon you; you are not permitted to exempt yourself (Yoma 67)." "<b>To walk in them.</b> Do not exempt yourself from among them — so that you do not say: I have learned the wisdom of Israel; I will go and learn the wisdom of the nations (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:56.631796904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}